{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5htunt","claim:pm-gh1699","claim:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-5htunt","lineage:pm-5oj5","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-5htunt+pm-gh1699+pm-nhauur","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5htunt","claim:pm-gh1699","claim:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-5htunt","lineage:pm-5oj5","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-pwqiao"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"files/docs --add refusal does not name the note segment it misread as a key, nor offer the standalone --note flag"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-10 while linking evidence for pm-5htunt. 'pm files <id> --add \"path=a.txt,scope=project,note=Single-label host, host:port, whitespace\"' exits with invalid_argument. The message says only 'Expected key=value entries separated by commas'. The cause is the deliberate pm-fr10t8 / GH-258 boundary: after a comma, the identifier-shaped segment 'host:port' is read as a new markdown-style key 'host', and an unknown key is refused strictly. Commas alone are accepted as note continuation ('a, b and c'), so an agent cannot tell from the refusal which segment broke the entry. The refusal also does not mention the standalone --note flag (pm-pfnx, GH-170), which takes free text with no parsing. Reproduced with the built CLI in a sandbox tracker. Duplicate check: searched 'files --add note colon comma csv key value parse'; pm-fr10t8 (closed) fixed non-identifier candidate keys and keeps this identifier case strict by design; pm-0v9k (closed) introduced strict rejection."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","files","parser","recovery"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":45},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A files/docs --add refusal caused by an unknown key from a continuation segment names that segment and key in details and in the message; The recovery offers the same link with the prose moved to the standalone --note flag (or a quoting form the parser accepts), and executing it links the file with the full note text; GH-258 strict rejection of identifier-shaped typo keys such as lable=main is unchanged"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-f05lsg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"The invalid_argument refusal names the segment and the unknown key it produced (here 'host' from ' host:port'), and offers an executable retry using --note for the free text."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-0v9k","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-5htunt","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-fr10t8","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-pfnx","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"d966dfc7f6da710a544db2d80ab314fbf9ede12fdc29e07cc5eabce79ded8eda","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5503f4d464682012b879f14affe93665956afd6f849dd34e7b0989ecacefaf4f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T16:58:21.477Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A files/docs --add refusal caused by an unknown key from a continuation segment names that segment and key in details and in the message; The recovery offers the same link with the prose moved to the standalone --note flag (or a quoting form the parser accepts), and executing it links the file with the full note text; GH-258 strict rejection of identifier-shaped typo keys such as lable=main is unchanged; Both refusal paths are covered, with tests for each variant: the generic invalid-entry refusal raised in parseCsvKv when a later segment follows a non-continuable key (the recorded example), and the unknown-key refusal when the note ends with the key-shaped segment (note=... host:port)"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T16:58:21.477Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-10 while linking evidence for pm-5htunt. 'pm files <id> --add \"path=a.txt,scope=project,note=Single-label host, host:port, whitespace\"' exits with invalid_argument and the message says only 'Expected key=value entries separated by commas'. Cause (src/core/item/parse.ts parseCsvKv; corrected after review on PR 1701): after a comma, the identifier-shaped segment 'host:port' opens a new markdown-style key 'host' (the pm-fr10t8 / GH-258 boundary keeps identifier-shaped keys strict). The next segment ' whitespace' has no delimiter, and 'host' is not a continuable key, so parseCsvKv throws the generic invalid-entry refusal; the unknown-key check (assertNoUnknownCsvKeys) is never reached. If the note ends with 'host:port' instead, the entry reaches the unknown-key refusal. Commas alone are accepted as note continuation ('a, b and c'), so an agent cannot tell from either refusal which segment broke the entry. Neither refusal mentions the standalone --note flag (pm-pfnx, GH-170), which takes free text with no parsing. Reproduced with the built CLI in a sandbox tracker. Duplicate check: searched 'files --add note colon comma csv key value parse'; pm-fr10t8 (closed) fixed non-identifier candidate keys and deliberately keeps the identifier case strict; pm-0v9k (closed) introduced strict rejection."}],"before_hash":"d966dfc7f6da710a544db2d80ab314fbf9ede12fdc29e07cc5eabce79ded8eda","after_hash":"67d6513b8da3ee84864c49bb1db575c7e4132b359b7d8beb63babc31896af1b5","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Correct the causal path and cover both refusal paths (review on PR 1701)","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"689b1f74ea1c54477c9098f5c03ce77f475750b008f0dc81c8c091afb09f1848"}
